---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const description = 'About Q.C. Zhang and the TCG / Configurable Universe research program.';

// JSON-LD Person schema — feeds Google Knowledge Graph
const personSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'Person',
	name: 'Q.C. Zhang',
	url: new URL('/', Astro.site).toString(),
	mainEntityOfPage: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).toString(),
	image: new URL('/og-image.png', Astro.site).toString(),
	jobTitle: 'Independent researcher in theoretical physics',
	email: 'mailto:qczhang@aya.yale.edu',
	knowsAbout: [
		'Theoretical physics',
		'Twistor theory',
		'Quantum gravity',
		'Cosmological constant',
		'Foundations of physics',
		'Configurable Universe',
		'Twistor Configuration Geometry',
	],
	subjectOf: [
		{ '@type': 'CreativeWork', name: 'Twistor Configuration Geometry research program', url: new URL('/papers/', Astro.site).toString() },
	],
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description} schema={personSchema} />
		<style>
			.page-header {
				padding: 3rem 1rem 1.5rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
				background: var(--bg-subtle);
			}
			.page-header-inner {
				max-width: var(--page-width);
				margin: 0 auto;
			}
			.page-eyebrow {
				font-family: var(--font-sans);
				font-size: 0.78rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				color: var(--accent);
				letter-spacing: 0.12em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
			}
			.page-header h1 {
				margin: 0 0 0.3em 0;
				font-size: 2.1rem;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			}
			.lede {
				font-family: var(--font-serif);
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-style: italic;
				margin: 0;
				line-height: 1.5;
				max-width: 600px;
			}
			main {
				max-width: var(--page-width);
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 2.5rem 1rem 1rem;
			}
			h2 {
				margin-top: 2.5em;
				font-size: 1.3rem;
			}
			.contact-card {
				margin-top: 3rem;
				padding: 1.5em 1.6em;
				background: var(--bg-subtle);
				border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
				border-radius: 6px;
			}
			.contact-card h3 {
				margin: 0 0 0.5em 0;
				font-size: 1rem;
			}
			.contact-card p {
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 0.95rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<div class="page-header">
			<div class="page-header-inner">
				<div class="page-eyebrow">About</div>
				<h1>Q.C. Zhang</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Independent researcher in theoretical physics.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<main>
			<p>
				My work proposes that the dimensionless constants of physics — α, Λ, α<sub>G</sub>,
				Yukawa couplings, sin²θ<sub>W</sub>, and others — are not free parameters but
				structural invariants of a combinatorial geometry built on Penrose's projective
				twistor space CP³.
			</p>

			<p>
				The framework is <strong>Twistor Configuration Geometry (TCG)</strong>; the
				philosophical reading is the <strong>Configurable Universe</strong> — constants
				are chamber invariants, in the same sense that the dimension of a vector space is.
			</p>

			<h2>Empirical anchor</h2>
			<p>
				Nine sub-percent algebraic relations among independently-measured constants,
				spanning <strong>124 orders of magnitude</strong> across six physical sectors —
				none currently derivable from the Standard Model or general relativity.
			</p>

			<h2>Falsifiable prediction</h2>
			<p>
				A spin-1 mediated short-range fifth force at α<sub>Y</sub> ≈ 1.88×10⁴, λ ≲ 5–10 μm —
				about 500× from current short-range gravity bounds. The framework also includes
				one no-go theorem (60σ on-shell weak-angle exclusion) and three structural
				constraints, listed in the <a href="/papers/04-predictions-no-go/">Predictions
				ledger</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>The corpus</h2>
			<p>
				Twenty-one papers on Zenodo, CC-BY-4.0: a seventeen-paper Twistor Configuration
				Geometry arc (synthesis, framework architecture, specific empirical predictions,
				and methodology) plus four adjacent workstreams. See the
				<a href="/papers/">full list</a>.
			</p>

			<div class="contact-card">
				<h3>Contact</h3>
				<p>
					Email: <a href="mailto:qczhang@aya.yale.edu">qczhang@aya.yale.edu</a>
				</p>
				<p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
					Open to criticism, collaboration, and pointers to related work.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
